/-!
# A cofiltered system of nonempty affine schemes with empty limit, in any universe

For a field `F`, the spectra of the subrings of `F` generated by finite subsets of `F`, indexed by
`(Finset F)ᵒᵖ`, form a cofiltered system of nonempty affine schemes with affine transition
morphisms. A family of compatible ring homomorphisms out of these subrings into a nonzero ring `A`
yields an injection of `F` into `A`; consequently every cone over the system whose vertex is too
small for `F` has empty vertex, and the empty scheme is a limit of the system when `F` is not
`u`-small.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.stageUniv`: a `Type u` copy of the subring of `F` generated by
  a finite set.
* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.schemeDiagramUniv`: the system of spectra of these rings.
* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.emptyConeUniv`: the cone over the system with empty vertex.
* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.isLimitEmptyConeUniv`: the empty cone is a limit cone when `F`
  is not `u`-small.

## Main results

* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.exists_injective_of_compatible_closureMaps`: compatible ring
  homomorphisms from the finitely generated subrings of a field `F` into a nonzero ring `A` give
  an injection `F → A`.
* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.isEmpty_cone_pt_of_mk_lt`: a cone over the system whose vertex
  has fewer global sections than `F` has elements has empty vertex.
* `Stacks.EmptyLimitCounterexample.isEmpty_limit_of_nonempty_stages_univ`: for `bigField`, the
  empty cone is a limit cone while every scheme of the system is nonempty.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

